laintext, trip 1", "encrypted, trip 1"], ["First app data", "after 2 RTT", "after 1 RTT"]], "ids": ["row-1", "row-2", "row-3", "row-4"]}, "says": [{"id": "why-one-round-trip-is-enough.1.1", "status": "ready", "text": "In TLS 1.2, the first trip only agreed on algorithms, and the key exchange needed a second trip. TLS 1.3 merges them: the client sends its key share up front, betting on a group. TLS 1.3 also trimmed the menu to a handful of strong groups, so the bet almost always wins. That's how the first application data arrives after one round trip.", "cues": [{"at": 16, "end": 26, "label": "first trip", "target": "row-1", "text": "", "kind": "row", "id": "row-1", "t": 2.237}, {"at": 62, "end": 74, "label": "key exchange", "target": "row-2", "text": "", "kind": "row", "id": "row-2", "t": 4.775}, {"at": 286, "end": 308, "label": "first application data", "target": "row-4", "text": "", "kind": "row", "id": "row-4", "t": 20.637}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/e6da9aecd667b070ebe802fa.mp3", "duration": 24.025, "words": [{"s": 0.3, "e": 0.438, "c0": 0, "c1": 2}, {"s": 0.438, "e": 1.038, "c0": 3, "c1": 6}, {"s": 1.038, "e": 2.0, "c0": 7, "c1": 10}, {"s": 2.125, "e": 2.237, "c0": 12, "c1": 15}, {"s": 2.237, "e": 2.5, "c0": 16, "c1": 21}, {"s": 2.5, "e": 2.775, "c0": 22, "c1": 26}, {"s": 2.775, "e": 3.075, "c0": 27, "c1": 31}, {"s": 3.075, "e": 3.413, "c0": 32, "c1": 38}, {"s": 3.413, "e": 3.55, "c0": 39, "c1": 41}, {"s": 3.55, "e": 4.475, "c0": 42, "c1": 52}, {"s": 4.575, "e": 4.688, "c0": 54, "c1": 57}, {"s": 4.688, "e": 4.775, "c0": 58, "c1": 61}, {"s": 4.775, "e": 5.0, "c0": 62, "c1": 65}, {"s": 5.0, "e": 5.575, "c0": 66, "c1": 74}, {"s": 5.575, "e": 5.862, "c0": 75, "c1": 81}, {"s": 5.862, "e": 5.938, "c0": 82, "c1": 83}, {"s": 5.938, "e": 6.275, "c0": 84, "c1": 90}, {"s": 6.275, "e": 6.925, "c0": 91, "c1": 95}, {"s": 7.075, "e": 7.662, "c0": 97, "c1": 100}, {"s": 7.662, "e": 8.4, "c0": 101, "c1": 104}, {"s": 8.4, "e": 8.75, "c0": 105, "c1": 111}, {"s": 8.