ke traffic secret", "MS": "Master Secret", "CATS": "client application traffic secret", "SATS": "server application traffic secret"}, "labels": [], "order": ["PSK", "ES", "DHE", "HS", "CHTS", "SHTS", "MS", "CATS", "SATS"]}, "says": [{"id": "where-the-keys-come-from.1.1", "status": "ready", "text": "Every key descends from one schedule built on HKDF. It starts with the early secret, made from a pre-shared key if resuming, or zeros otherwise. Mixing in the Diffie-Hellman shared secret gives the handshake secret. From it come two traffic secrets, one per direction, that encrypt the server's flight and the client's Finished. One more step gives the master secret, and from that the application traffic secrets for real data.", "cues": [{"at": 71, "end": 83, "label": "early secret", "target": "ES", "text": "Early Secret", "kind": "node", "id": "ES", "t": 4.625}, {"at": 159, "end": 187, "label": "Diffie-Hellman shared secret", "target": "DHE", "text": "ECDHE shared secret", "kind": "node", "id": "DHE", "t": 10.275}, {"at": 198, "end": 214, "label": "handshake secret", "target": "HS", "text": "Handshake Secret", "kind": "node", "id": "HS", "t": 12.025}, {"at": 286, "end": 301, "label": "server's flight", "target": "SHTS", "text": "server handshake traffic secret", "kind": "node", "id": "SHTS", "t": 17.188}, {"at": 310, "end": 327, "label": "client's Finished", "target": "CHTS", "text": "client handshake traffic secret", "kind": "node", "id": "CHTS", "t": 18.3}, {"at": 353, "end": 366, "label": "master secret", "target": "MS", "text": "Master Secret", "kind": "node", "id": "MS", "t": 20.975}, {"at": 386, "end": 413, "label": "application traffic secrets", "target": "CATS", "text": "client application traffic secret", "kind": "node", "id": "CATS", "t": 22.825}], "notes": [], "code": [], "audio": "audio/1bf3b9b42b1e48bb735a8495.mp3", "duration": 25.675, "words": [{"s": 0.275, "e": 0.562, "c0": 0, "c1": 5}, {"s": 0.562, "e": 0.8, "c0": 6, "c1": 9}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 1.25, "c0": 10